   "status": "done",
   "note": "Article runs pp. 31–40 (PDF 51–60), the whole of ch. 3. Three things to check against the scan: (1) p. 38 (PDF 58): the printed text gives 'Primo … prestaret… Tertio' with no second reason for Christ's baptism; kept, with a translator's note. (2) p. 34 (PDF 54): 'in Luca fertur Christum verba ista dixisse ad turbas', though in Luke 3:7 it is John who speaks; kept as printed, with a note. (3) p. 32 (PDF 52): 'de duris et crudis pellicearum minutiis' (John's girdle) is uncertain in the OCR. Denis reads 'ad radicem arboris' (singular) at 3:10, so the lemma marker stops at 'the root of the' and 'tree' follows outside it. The closing questions go back over the chapter (rebaptism tagged v. 6; the dove and the voice vv. 16–17)."
  },
