   "note": "Article runs pp. 40–46 (PDF 60–66), Matt 4:1–11; starts at the foot of PDF 60 (pre-split OCR: heading at the bottom of the left column). Two readings to check against the scan: (1) p. 42 (PDF 62): the Greek word after 'nomen Domini' is garbled in the OCR ('ceceayeziuxzov'); read as τετραγράμματον (same length, fits the sense). (2) p. 46 (PDF 66): 'Qui quia diabolus dicit se posse dare' kept as printed in the OCR, though 'Quæ' would fit better; translated by the sense. Eccles 3:21 and Prov 21:30 are quoted in variant forms (marked with Douay wording, translator's note gives Denis's reading). The closing moral paragraphs go back over the chapter (tags vv. 10, 1–3, 4–10, 8)."
  },
