   "status": "done",
   "note": "Article runs pp. 47–50 (PDF 67–70), Matt 4:12–25. Denis reads 4:16 as 'Populus qui ambulabat in tenebris' (Isaias 9:2's wording; Vulgate Matthew has 'sedebat'): marked with the Douay wording, 'walked' kept outside the marker, with a translator's note. p. 48 (PDF 68): the edition prints an asterisk after 'sedentibus' (footnote not in the OCR); kept as printed. OCR readings to check against the scan: p. 50 (PDF 70) 'Crebra namque et magna prodigia' (OCR 'lebra'), 'obtulerunt ei' (OCR 'et'). Matt 11:21 is quoted in reverse order ('Væ tibi, Bethsaida; væ tibi, Corozain') and the Douay-Rheims file reads 'Woe thee, Corozain', so 'to' sits outside the marker. The marginal reference for Josaphat reads 'I Par. xvii' in the OCR; the passage is 2 Par 17:7–9. The closing paragraphs (Jerome on the fishermen, the mystical sense of the four names, prelates visiting their flock) go back over the chapter (tags vv. 18–22, 18–22, 23)."
  },
